From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rt5645: Perform the initial jack detect at probe

A card described with simple-audio-card has no machine driver, so nothing
calls rt5645_set_jack_detect() and nothing performs the initial jack
detect - its closing rt5645_irq(0, rt5645) is the only caller. Jack state
is then only ever sampled from an edge on hp-detect-gpios.

So a headphone already in the socket at boot is never noticed, and the
card is silent with every mixer control set correctly and every register
on the DAC path reading right. rt5645_jack_detect() is what force enables
the "LDO2" and "Mic Det Power" supplies that the "HP amp" widget depends
on, and what programs RT5645_CHARGE_PUMP away from its 0x0c06 reset value;
without it "HP amp" cannot power up. Physically unplugging and replugging
the jack fixes it, which is not a reasonable thing to ask of a user.

Do the initial detect at the end of the component probe when the driver
owns a hp-detect GPIO and the codec's own jack detect is not in use, which
is exactly the case that has no other trigger. A machine driver calling
rt5645_set_jack_detect() later simply repeats the detect, which is
harmless.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/rt5645.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/rt5645.c b/sound/soc/codecs/rt5645.c
index e9819653b30d..140957216e2b 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/rt5645.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/rt5645.c
@@ -3496,6 +3496,20 @@ static int rt5645_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	if (!rt5645->eq_param)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/*
+	 * Perform the initial jack detect if nothing else will. Only
+	 * rt5645_set_jack_detect() does so, and a card described with
+	 * simple-audio-card has no machine driver to call it, so jack state
+	 * would only ever be sampled from an edge on hp-detect-gpios.
+	 * A headphone already in the socket at boot is then never noticed:
+	 * the "LDO2" and "Mic Det Power" supplies that "HP amp" depends on
+	 * are never force enabled and the charge pump keeps its reset
+	 * value, so the output stays silent until the jack is physically
+	 * unplugged and replugged.
+	 */
+	if (!rt5645->pdata.jd_mode && rt5645->gpiod_hp_det)
+		rt5645_irq(0, rt5645);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
